  "body": "Opportunities to secure a substantial family home in this tightly held pocket of Takapuna are increasingly difficult to find — particularly at this level.\r\n\r\nPositioned in one of Takapuna’s most exclusive coastal streets, 2 Minnehaha Avenue offers an exceptional combination of location, land, size and flexibility. With Thorne Bay at the end of the street and Lake Pupuke directly across the road, this is a location where properties are tightly held and opportunities to buy are limited.\r\n\r\nImportantly, the current price point represents a comparatively low entry level for a property of this size in such a premium position. Our vendors are serious about achieving a sale and are calling for all genuine offers to be presented.\r\n\r\nFor buyers who have been waiting for an opportunity to secure a substantial home in the Minnehaha/Thorne Bay precinct, this property demands inspection.\r\n\r\nPROPERTY FEATURES\r\n\r\n• Prime 594sqm freehold site (more or less)\r\n• Five double bedrooms\r\n• Ground-floor master suite with ensuite and walk-in wardrobe\r\n• Self-contained accommodation above the garage with its own kitchen and lounge\r\n• Three further double bedrooms upstairs\r\n• Recently repainted internally\r\n• New carpets and updated lighting\r\n• Modern kitchen with large island/breakfast bar\r\n• Formal lounge with open fireplace\r\n• Large separate dining room ideal for entertaining\r\n• Recently completed hard landscaping\r\n• Thorne Bay Beach at the end of the street\r\n• Lake Pupuke directly across the road\r\n• Easy walk to both Takapuna and Milford shops, cafés, restaurants and amenities\r\n• One of Takapuna’s most tightly held and sought-after coastal locations\r\n• Zoned for both Westlake and Takapuna Grammar schools\r\n\r\nIf you have been considering Minnehaha Avenue, Thorne Bay or the wider Golden Mile, now is the time to act. Flexible viewing times daily.\r\n\r\nIf you can’t reach Andrew Dorreen, please contact his Sales Associate, Anna Jones, on 021 489 171.",
